/target
/wt/target
/threads-spike/target
# regenerable fixtures/corpus (see `cargo run --bin genfixture` / `gencorpus`)
*.temenc
/corpus
/corpus.json
# scratch wasm patches
patched*.wasm
# Playwright (the real-browser test harness) is installed fresh in CI, not vendored.
/node_modules
/package.json
/package-lock.json
# on-ramp playground assets built by `build-onramp-assets.mjs` (regenerable). The tiny
# `hello_c.temen` is committed so the playground has a working example out of the box; the big
# guests (Lua/SQLite) are built on demand / by the Pages pipeline.
/web/assets/*.bc
/web/assets/*.ll
/web/assets/*.temen
/web/assets/*.wad
/web/assets/*.img
!/web/assets/hello_c.temen
# nim_hello.temen — a real Nim program (`write(stdout, "hello, svm")`) compiled through nimony →
# temen-leng → the nim→powerbox bridge to a runnable module, committed like `hello_c` so the "run real
# Nim" playground card works out of the box. Regenerate with `cargo run -p temen-run --example
# build_nim_hello_temen` (needs the nimony toolchain); gated by `crates/temen-run/tests/nim_hello_asset.rs`.
!/web/assets/nim_hello.temen
!/web/assets/gradient.temen
!/web/assets/bounce.temen
!/web/assets/life.temen
!/web/assets/mandelzoom.temen
# QuickJS is committed prebuilt: its build needs a guest libm (openlibm) fetched from GitHub, which
# the Pages pipeline can't reach — so the translated `.temen` ships in-tree (like `hello_c`) and the
# playground's JS demo works out of the box. `build-onramp-assets.mjs` rebuilds it in place when the
# sources *are* fetchable, and otherwise leaves this committed artifact untouched.
!/web/assets/qjs_repl.temen
# qjs_snapshot.temen — the two-phase (`main`/`warmup`/`eval_run`) QuickJS driver for the WASM_AOT.md
# warm-runtime snapshot (`temen_warm_*`), committed prebuilt for the same fetch-gated reason as
# `qjs_repl.temen`. `build-onramp-assets.mjs` rebuilds it in place when the sources are fetchable; the
# committed `warm-snapshot-test.mjs` uses it (and skips cleanly if absent).
!/web/assets/qjs_snapshot.temen
# lua_snapshot.temen — the two-phase (`main`/`warmup`/`eval_run`) Lua 5.4.7 driver for the warm-runtime
# snapshot (issue #805), committed prebuilt like `qjs_snapshot.temen` so the warm Lua card + the
# `snapshot-worker-test.mjs` browser test work out of the box (browser-real runs on committed assets
# only). A generated binary asset (like the vendored `doom1.wad`): regenerate from
# `lua_snapshot_harness.c` via the recipe in crates/temen-llvm/tests/fixtures/lua/README.md and commit it —
# the ~76k-line intermediate `.ll` is NOT committed (no Rust test consumes it, unlike `lua_eval.ll`).
!/web/assets/lua_snapshot.temen
# chibicc (the in-browser C compiler, SELFHOST_C.md §7 step 5) is committed prebuilt for the same
# reason: `build-onramp-assets.mjs` builds it fail-soft (skipped when clang/llvm-18 is absent or the
# build hiccups), so relying on the deploy-time build alone silently ships a 404 (the I26/I42 class).
# Shipping the translated `.temen` in-tree makes the C-compiler card work out of the box; the build
# script rebuilds it in place when the toolchain is present.
!/web/assets/chibicc.temen
# temen-leng (the in-browser leng→TEMEN-IR self-host card, NIM.md §3e) is committed prebuilt for the same
# reason: it's a copy of the in-tree `crates/temen-run/demos/leng_selfhost/temen-leng.temen` asset (whose own
# code-coupling gate keeps it in sync), so the self-host card works out of the box even when the
# `-Z build-std`/`llvm-18` toolchain that rebuilds it is absent. `build-onramp-assets.mjs` copies it.
!/web/assets/temen-leng.temen
